# ProPo governance

Repository: Vedang1998/Stocky
Application: stocky-plus/
Product: ProPo
Legal entity: IVYY LLC (owner supplied)

Read stocky-plus/docs/agents/PROPO_AUTONOMOUS_DELIVERY_PROTOCOL.md
with AGENTS.md. Its new rules require the introducing governance PR's
acceptance and owner merge; do not move a frozen review subject to adopt it.
Even after that merge, protocol §5 bounded merge delegation stays INACTIVE
until a separately reviewed activation package is owner-approved. Loading
this protocol does not activate it, and activation cannot be inferred from
protocol text.
If this tool also loads CLAUDE.md, the Claude reviewer role does not make
Cursor an actual Claude reviewer. Record the real tool/model/run and role.

Before substantial work, read:
1. AGENTS.md
2. stocky-plus/docs/README.md
3. stocky-plus/docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md
4. Active phase records
5. Relevant approved product documents

Authority:
- ChatGPT owns product decisions, architecture, scope, acceptance criteria,
  phase control, merge recommendations and agent coordination.
- Cursor implements only approved scope.
- Claude Code independently reviews.
- The user alone authorizes merges after ChatGPT acceptance. That is the
  CURRENT merge rule. Proposed protocol §5 delegation is not active.
- GitHub is the permanent project record.

Hard boundaries:
- Never commit directly to main.
- Never mark a PR ready or merge without explicit authorization.
- Never begin a later or dependent PR or phase early. ChatGPT may
  authorize only contract-frozen, dependency-independent lanes under
  stocky-plus/docs/ACCELERATED_SAFE_DELIVERY.md. Future-phase runtime,
  migrations, Shopify configuration, production actions, and other
  dependent work remain gated.
- Never claim a command, test, CI run, build, migration, repository state,
  deployment or external fact without direct evidence.
- Never access production or merchant data without explicit authorization.
- Never deploy or execute a production backfill without explicit authorization.
- Never enable inventory-write flags without explicit authorization.
- Never mutate Shopify inventory unless separately approved.
- Never commit secrets, credentials, .env files, customer data or production data.

Approved product documents override:
- unfinished code;
- old prompts;
- README claims;
- implementation convenience;
- model assumptions.
